WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.180
The UN calls a planned US firing squad livestream torture. This is Omni View North America, episode 16. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Defense officials say Army psychiatrist Nadal Hassan will face a firing squad, with the execution sent out live in the details still to come. He killed 13 people on a US base in 2009. The Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights told AFP a livestream would count as a public execution and would break the absolute ban on torture.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.000
That office said it has used the same words for public executions in Afghanistan and Iran,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.540
calling them cruel, inhuman, or degrading treatment or punishment.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.720
Robin M. Maher of the Death Penalty Information Center told the Guardian she knows of no

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.860
rule or precedent for putting a military execution on the Internet for a wide public.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.620
She said public executions are typically how authoritarian governments spread fear and

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.360
display control.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.980
And the Guardian reported members of Congress calling the plan grotesque and likening

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:01.860
to tactics of some terror groups and oppressive governments. Across the region, a fuel tax

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.420
fight that was still a call for relief at the start of the month is now statute in North Carolina.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.000
Governor Josh Stein signed it Friday, lifting the 41-cent state tax on gasoline and diesel

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.560
through November 30. WRAL says the break is expected to cost more than $350 million that normally

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.340
pays for road work at the Department of Transportation. The statute refills that budget from

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:28.500
savings of about $11 billion. The station said pump prices have stayed high since President

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.260
Donald Trump launched an attack on Iran earlier this year.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:36.040
It takes effect Saturday, but fuel already taxed and sitting in station tanks could hold

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:41.660
prices up for days or weeks. In Alberta, Lager asked 1,000 people early this month and found

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:47.000
70 percent want to remain in Canada against 22 percent who want a separation process to begin.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.520
The Edmonton Journal column says the pollster found 77 percent very likely to vote above

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.240
of the 50 to 60% who usually commit to a ballot

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.980
in a provincial or federal election.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.480
Edmonton split 80% stay to 13% leave.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.740
Calgary 66 to 22.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.280
The rest of the province 62 to 30.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:08.160
Stay option voters were 91% firm.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:11.220
Separatist option voters 71%.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.840
Gunter wrote that those interviews came before word

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.120
that Alberta Prosperity Project members had met

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.120
in secret with Trump administration officials

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.240
and Republican operatives and had apparently offered oil

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.760
and fresh water for American help winning independence.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:28.640
Also today, the Cook Political Report shifted 18 House seats toward Democrats.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.620
The Hill reported, including seats held by Republicans Marionette Miller-Meks and Zack

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.280
Nunn of Iowa and Ryan McKenzie of Pennsylvania.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.600
WIS says the state law enforcement division arrested South Carolina Democrat Michael Rivers

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.300
on Friday for pointing and presenting a firearm.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:50.180
He was released on a $15,000 bond, and lawyer Seth Rose says he asserts innocence and that

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:54.860
a political opponent brought the accusation. A Pew Research Survey released Thursday found

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.560
30 percent approved of President Trump's job performance, and 68 percent disapproved.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:04.320
The Hill reported. The New York Times says the FBI arrested a key suspect in the shiny

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:09.060
hunter's hack of its own agents' data after a group threatened to expose agents' personal

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:14.180
information and left the bureau both victim and investigator. In the wider world, Secretary

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.460
of State Marker Rubio announced Friday that the United States is imposing full blocking

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.500
sanctions on the International Criminal Court.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:24.960
The Hill said the step sharply escalates Washington's fight with the court over criticism

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.920
that it is unjustly pursuing war crimes cases against Israel, American service members,

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.180
and the Trump administration.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:35.980
The Hill reported that the sanctions announcement coincided with a Nobel Peace Prize awarded

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:36.460
to a judge.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.340
The case on both sides of North Carolina's fuel tax break is whether it is driver relief

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.600
or a campaign calendar.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.520
Senate leader Phil Berger said people need real relief and need it now.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:51.160
After Republican leaders called a special session on October 3, while lawmakers were on

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:51.420
break.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:56.700
Democrats say Republicans suspended the tax not only to save drivers money, but also to

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.860
help their reelection chances, pointing to that session's timing and to an end date

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:01.760
of November 30.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:07.800
In a year when all 170 General Assembly seats are up, Michael Bitzer of Kataba College said

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.700
economic factors are likely to drag Republicans down, and that Republicans have voiced concern

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:13.700
about losing influence.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:18.300
A high-point university poll released late last month put President Trump's approval

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.280
at 43 percent among likely voters in North Carolina.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.980
What both sides accept is that the bill passed with overwhelming support from both parties

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:27.920
and that the suspension is temporary.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:33.160
A sign of progress in Montreal, two people repairing windows are safely on the ground after

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.000
their platform failed and left them hanging several stories up.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.680
Global News says, that's OmniView North America for today.

